      "statusChangeID": "6849d1716e43ed5ac11a3be5",
      "statusChangeNewStatus": "complete",
      "value": "This one turned out to be a bit of a journey, and nothing to do with Safari at all! It looks like for Safari you (or whoever sent it to you) must've copied that group code from a group/user profile somewhere, which meant it was subject to our character sanitization, which replaced the \".\" with a subtly different character. Our group search function wasn't tolerant of this, and so did a generic search rather than searching by group code. We've now updated our groups code to accept these technically-incorrect but our-fault group codes as well. Thanks for the report!",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
